humanizer — https://github.com/blader/humanizer
Copyright (c) blader. MIT License.

Adapted in release 1.6.0 into references/writing-rules.md (section 2 groups 1-7,
and the structural moves and two-pass audit in section 6) and into the metric
definitions M9-M11 in references/eval-rubric.md.

What was taken: the categorisation of AI-writing tells, the English blocklists
(significance inflation, promotional register, high-frequency AI vocabulary,
filler phrases with their replacements, authority tropes, signposting, fake-candid
openers), and the two-pass audit method — rewrite, then ask the draft what makes
it obviously AI-generated, then rewrite again.

D-DIN — https://www.datto.com/fonts/d-din
Copyright (c) 2017 Datto Inc., with Reserved Font Name "D-DIN".
SIL Open Font License 1.1 — full text in assets/fonts/COPYING.txt.

Vendored unmodified as assets/fonts/D-DIN.woff2 and D-DIN-Bold.woff2 because
design-rules.md requires the display face to be embedded in every deliverable,
and a release that declared it without shipping it rendered nothing. The OFL
permits redistribution provided the font is not sold on its own and the license
travels with it; the Reserved Font Name restricts derivatives, and none are made
here. Regenerate the embed block with scripts/build/embed_font.py.

Lucide — https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide
Copyright (c) for portions of Lucide are held by Cole Bemis 2013-2022
as part of Feather (MIT); all other copyright (c) Lucide Contributors 2022. ISC License — full text in
assets/icons/lucide/LICENSE.

Vendored in release 1.8.0 as assets/icons/lucide/, 2007 icons from lucide-static
v1.28.0, together with the project's tags.json so the set is searchable. The
files are reformatted only: comments stripped, whitespace collapsed, and the
baked width/height/class attributes removed so the host document sizes and
colours them. No path data is altered. The ISC licence permits redistribution
with the copyright notice, which travels in assets/icons/lucide/LICENSE.

Why a library rather than a house set: design-rules.md §5 required an embedded
semantic icon library from 1.2 and the package shipped none, so deliverables
carried zero icons. Release 1.8.0 first shipped eight hand-drawn icons, and a
reader found the expressiveness short and the icons poorly matched to the
content — eight meanings cannot cover a twenty-five page deck, so they were
reused for meanings they did not fit. Breadth is what fixes that, and drawing
two thousand icons by hand is not a design language, it is a second project.
LUMI's own contribution is the reserved bindings in scripts/build/embed_icons.py,
which pin one icon per recurring LUMI meaning. Re-vendor by fetching the
lucide-static tarball from the npm registry and re-running the same reformatting.

What was not taken from humanizer, and why: it is a general-purpose prose rewriter and
English-only. Rules that conflict with LUMI's fact discipline were dropped, its
patterns were re-scoped to LUMI's sales and marketing deliverables, and nothing
from it applies to Chinese output, which is governed instead by the
de-translationese pass in references/writing-rules.md section 6b. The skill itself
is not vendored, installed, or invoked; only its rules were adapted, so this
repository remains a single source of truth with no runtime dependency.

Natural Earth — https://www.naturalearthdata.com/
Public domain. The project asks for credit and does not require it.

Vendored as assets/vectors/upstream/ne_110m_admin_0_countries.geojson, the 110m
admin-0 country set, unmodified. The LUMI globe needs country-level boundaries,
which the hand-written coastlines in scripts/build/build_geography.py cannot express:
those are a two-degree stylisation for a cover mark and cannot say "these 27
countries are one region". The file is vendored rather than fetched so that
scripts/build/build_worldmap.py never touches the network and its --check is
reproducible offline. Regenerate assets/vectors/world-110m.json by running that
script.

At this scale the upstream set has no Singapore, Hong Kong, Bahrain or Malta;
the source merges them away, this repository does not drop them. They ship as
points in assets/vectors/regions.json instead, which is what a port is anyway.
